{%- comment -%}
  ─── THE PRICE BLOCK: ONE SNIPPET FOR THE GRID CARD AND THE PRODUCT VIEW ─────

  Junid's mockup (14 Nov 2026): RRP struck through in grey, the selling price
  big and red, and "SAVE R x" in a red outlined box, with a red "-NN%" pill.
  The grid card, the quick-view panel and the product page all render THIS
  file, so the three can never drift apart.

  EVERY NUMBER IS COMPUTED HERE from the variant's own price and compare-at
  price. Nothing is hardcoded to 65: the RRP is set per product by the
  reconciler (scripts/shopify/priceSync.mjs → rrpFor, 65% or 70% chip), and
  rounding it up to a "…99" gives cheap items 66–75%. The percent is whole-cent
  integer division, so it rounds DOWN and never overstates the saving.

  NO RRP (compare-at absent, zero, or not above the price) → the red price only:
  no pill, no strike-through, no SAVE box.

  ACCEPTS
    product   (required)
    variant   the variant to price; defaults to selected_or_first_available_variant
    layout    'card'  — grid: RRP line, price, SAVE box, stacked and centred
              'view'  — product view: price + RRP on one line, YOU SAVE box below
              'badge' — just the pill, "-65%"           (grid photo, top-left)
              'badge_off' — just the pill, "-65% OFF"   (product view title row)

  Colours and sizes live in marathon-storefront.css as tokens (--mc-pb-*,
  --mc-sale, --mc-rrp); nothing here is inline.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pb_layout = layout | default: 'card'
  assign pb_variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign pb_price = pb_variant.price | default: 0
  assign pb_compare = pb_variant.compare_at_price | default: 0
  assign pb_on_sale = false
  assign pb_off = 0
  if pb_price > 0 and pb_compare > pb_price
    assign pb_on_sale = true
    assign pb_save = pb_compare | minus: pb_price
    assign pb_off = pb_save | times: 100 | divided_by: pb_compare
  endif

  # Plain "R 2,499.00" everywhere, as in the mockup, deliberately NOT
  # money_with_currency: the shop's "show currency code" setting is on, and
  # "R 2,499.00 ZAR" three times in one small block is noise. The grid tile
  # already used plain money; the product page now matches it.
  assign pb_now_m = pb_price | money
  assign pb_rrp_m = pb_compare | money
  assign pb_save_m = pb_save | money
-%}
{%- case pb_layout -%}
  {%- when 'badge' -%}
    {%- if pb_on_sale -%}<span class="mc-pb-badge" data-mc-pb-badge>-{{ pb_off }}%</span>{%- endif -%}
  {%- when 'badge_off' -%}
    {%- if pb_on_sale -%}<span class="mc-pb-badge mc-pb-badge--view" data-mc-pb-badge>-{{ pb_off }}% OFF</span>{%- endif -%}
  {%- when 'view' -%}
    <div class="mc-pb mc-pb--view{% if pb_on_sale %} mc-pb--rrp{% endif %}" data-mc-pb data-mc-pb-off="{{ pb_off }}">
      <p class="mc-pb__row">
        <span class="visually-hidden">Price</span>
        <span class="mc-pb__now" data-mc-price-now>{{ pb_now_m }}</span>
        {%- if pb_on_sale %}
          <span class="mc-pb__rrp"><span class="mc-pb__rrp-label">RRP</span> <s class="mc-pb__rrp-price">{{ pb_rrp_m }}</s></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
      {%- if pb_on_sale -%}
        <p class="mc-pb__save"><span>You save {{ pb_save_m }}</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="mc-pb mc-pb--card{% if pb_on_sale %} mc-pb--rrp{% endif %}" data-mc-pb data-mc-pb-off="{{ pb_off }}">
      {%- if pb_on_sale -%}
        <p class="mc-pb__rrp"><span class="mc-pb__rrp-label">RRP</span> <s class="mc-pb__rrp-price">{{ pb_rrp_m }}</s></p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="mc-pb__now"><span class="visually-hidden">Price </span><span data-mc-price-now>{{ pb_now_m }}</span></p>
      {%- if pb_on_sale -%}
        <p class="mc-pb__save" data-mc-pb-save><span>Save {{ pb_save_m }}</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
{%- endcase -%}
